{"complete":true,"city":"Durban","template_id":"global-neighborhoods-one-reason","title":"10 Neighborhoods, One Reason Each","description":"Ten Durban localities, each anchored by one specific institution, landscape, or recurring event.","icon":"location_city","cards":[{"entity_name":"Berea","title":"Berea","subtitle":"For Africa’s oldest surviving botanic garden","notes":"Durban Botanic Gardens occupies 15 hectares on the Berea side of the city centre.","short_summary":"The neighborhood’s botanic garden conserves indigenous and exotic plant collections, including cycads, palms, bromeliads, and orchids.","source_url":"https://dag.durban.gov.za/storage/Documents/METRO%20Ezasegagasini%202025/Ezasegagasini%20Metro%20English%2019Sep2025.pdf","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — “Spring Has Sprung in the City’s Blossoming Gardens”","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Morningside","title":"Morningside","subtitle":"For a municipal park with a walk-through aviary","notes":"Mitchell Park combines picnic lawns and a children’s play area with its small zoo park.","short_summary":"The zoo park’s animal collection includes birds housed in a walk-through aviary.","source_url":"https://dag.durban.gov.za/storage/Documents/METRO%20Ezasegagasini%202025/Ezasegagasini%20Metro%20English%2019Sep2025.pdf","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — “Spring Has Sprung in the City’s Blossoming Gardens”","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Durban North","title":"Durban North","subtitle":"For the paths and ponds of the Japanese Gardens","notes":"The municipal garden’s walking paths circle ponds planted with water lilies.","short_summary":"Japanese-style ponds and a network of walking paths give this locality a distinct public garden.","source_url":"https://dag.durban.gov.za/storage/Documents/METRO%20Ezasegagasini%202025/Ezasegagasini%20Metro%20English%2019Sep2025.pdf","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — “Spring Has Sprung in the City’s Blossoming Gardens”","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"North Beach","title":"North Beach","subtitle":"For a garden between the promenade and the hotels","notes":"Amphitheatre Gardens sits on the Golden Mile between the beachfront promenade and the hotel strip.","short_summary":"Its ponds, fountains, and subtropical planting form a small landscaped pause beside the beachfront.","source_url":"https://dag.durban.gov.za/storage/Documents/METRO%20Ezasegagasini%202025/Ezasegagasini%20Metro%20English%2019Sep2025.pdf","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — “Spring Has Sprung in the City’s Blossoming Gardens”","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Glenwood","title":"Glenwood","subtitle":"For a nonprofit contemporary-art space","notes":"KZNSA Gallery operates from Bulwer Road as a nonprofit devoted to advancing visual art.","short_summary":"Its exhibition program gives Glenwood a standing address for contemporary visual art.","source_url":"https://kznsagallery.co.za/","source_title":"KZNSA Gallery — Home","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Yellowwood Park","title":"Yellowwood Park","subtitle":"For a 210-hectare protected area inside the suburb","notes":"Kenneth Stainbank Nature Reserve is situated within Yellowwood Park, southwest of central Durban.","short_summary":"A substantial protected landscape is embedded directly in this residential locality.","source_url":"https://www.kznwildlife.com/downloads/03-Management-Plans/Approved/2015%20-%20Kenneth%20Stainbank%20Nature%20Reserve%20Management%20Plan.pdf","source_title":"Ezemvelo KZN Wildlife — Kenneth Stainbank Nature Reserve Management Plan","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Inanda","title":"Inanda","subtitle":"For Gandhi’s Phoenix Settlement","notes":"The settlement was established in 1904 and later became home to the press that published Indian Opinion.","short_summary":"Phoenix Settlement preserves a documented site from Gandhi’s years in South Africa.","source_url":"https://www.phoenixsettlement.co.za/word/about/","source_title":"Phoenix Settlement Trust — About Phoenix Settlement","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Greyville","title":"Greyville","subtitle":"For the annual Durban July","notes":"The Durban July is staged at Hollywoodbets Greyville Racecourse on Avondale Road.","short_summary":"Greyville’s namesake racecourse is the fixed venue for Durban’s annual July race meeting.","source_url":"https://visitdurban.travel/event/hollywoodbets-durban-july-2026","source_title":"Durban Tourism — Hollywoodbets Durban July 2026","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Durban Central","title":"Durban Central","subtitle":"For natural-science galleries inside City Hall","notes":"The first-floor museum presents public natural-science galleries and curriculum-linked programs.","short_summary":"Durban Natural Science Museum places a public science collection within the civic center.","source_url":"https://www.durban.gov.za/page/parks-recreation-culture-amenities","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — Parks, Recreation & Culture Amenities","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Westville","title":"Westville","subtitle":"For a municipal local-history museum","notes":"Bergtheil Museum is one of eThekwini’s managed Local History Museum sites and stands on Queens Avenue.","short_summary":"Westville has its own branch in the municipality’s local-history museum network.","source_url":"https://www.durban.gov.za/page/parks-recreation-culture-amenities","source_title":"eThekwini Municipality — Parks, Recreation & Culture Amenities","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null}],"warnings":[]}
